{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_1443662647#9_2986458590","relevance":2,"reason":"The passage provides supporting evidence that disability insurance is worth considering because it replaces income, one in four workers become disabled before retirement, and illness makes disability coverage broader than AD&D. However, the document is primarily about whether AD&D insurance is worth it, not dedicated to why disability insurance is a smart investment.","learned":"Disability insurance can be a stronger investment than AD&D because it covers income loss from illness as well as injury, while AD&D has narrower payout limitations."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"long-term disability insurance\" \"worth having\" \"income protection\")","reason":"Search for more dedicated long-term disability insurance articles that directly answer it is worth having and explain the income-protection rationale."}}
