{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_2009951134#4_3284906218","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment from a focused individual disability insurance quotes page with an explicit 'Long-Term Disability Insurance Quotes Good Investment' section. It supports the investment rationale by discussing premium factors, the advantage that young people pay lower premiums, and whether purchasing coverage is the best decision for a family.","learned":"Repeated evidence: disability insurance can be financially smart to buy earlier because younger applicants may pay lower premiums, and coverage decisions should be weighed against family income-protection needs."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"disability income insurance\" \"worth it\" (+ income paycheck earnings))","reason":"Search a related phrase, 'disability income insurance,' to find additional dedicated worth-it articles beyond already-seen disability insurance pages, focused on protecting income or earnings."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"disability income insurance\" \"worth it\" (+ income paycheck earnings))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_13_226485794#9_523416185","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1183","rank":1,"snippet":"\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_13_226485794#9_523416185\" , \"end_char\": 6393.000000 , \"headings\": \"Understanding life insurance policy riders Understanding life insurance policy riders Does “one size fits all” apply to life insurance? What is a rider on a whole life insurance policy? More insurance coverage Unexpected misfortune Special circumstances Discover more from MassMutual... Need Advice? Contact us \" , \"segment\": \"Many insurance professionals suggest looking at other options, like disability income insurance, before adding such riders. ( Related: Is <cover>disability income insurance worth it? ) </cover>Riders are also becoming more widely available to help people get through problems in later years, like the need for long-term care or facing a terminal illness. Generally, these riders allow policyowners to accelerate the payment of death benefits to help cover care or end-of-life costs. This option will reduce both the policy and any riders eligible to be accelerated in proportion to the amount of the accelerated death benefit ; and typically, has an additional cost when exercised. Also important to note, while a life insurance policy that allows death benefits to be accelerated to "}}
