{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_268885785#3_651177914","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment from a dedicated disability insurance article. It directly states that disability insurance protects your paycheck if illness or injury makes you unable to work, supporting the smart-investment rationale of protecting income against disability risk.","learned":"Repeated Business Insider evidence: disability insurance is important because it protects paychecks and income when illness or injury prevents work."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"disability insurance\" \"odds of becoming disabled\" income)","reason":"Search for dedicated disability insurance pages using disability-risk statistics and income protection, likely to provide direct evidence that coverage is a smart investment because disability is more common than people expect."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"disability insurance\" \"odds of becoming disabled\" income)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_355237211#6_557845532","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1187","rank":1,"snippet":"Insurance Life Insurance Quotes \" , \"segment\": \"You choose the term, such as 5, 10, 20 or 30 years, and the amount of coverage you need when you get life insurance quotes. Once the term ends, the coverage ends. If there are no ongoing financial obligations as part of a divorce agreement, then it may make sense to remove an ex-spouse as a beneficiary on an existing life insurance policy. 2. Disability insurance<cover>Disability insurance pays a portion of your income if you can’t work because of an injury or illness. It’s often overlooked, yet financial experts rank it up there with life insurance as an important financial priority. The odds of becoming disabled </cover>for 90 days or more are greater than dying before retirement. Today's 20-year-olds have a 1 in 8 chance of dying before reaching age 67 and a more than 1 in 4 chance of becoming disabled, according to the Social Security Administration. Couples should plan for disability insurance before the divorce is final, the American Institute of CPAs says. It’s a good idea to have disability coverage of your own if you earn an income."}}
{"request":{"judgments":"39/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_355237211#6_557845532","relevance":2,"reason":"The passage directly supports why disability insurance is financially important: it pays part of income if injury or illness prevents work, is ranked by experts with life insurance as a priority, and disability before retirement is more likely than death. However, the document appears to be a broader financial/insurance-planning article rather than dedicated to why disability insurance is a smart investment.","learned":"Supporting evidence: disability insurance is often an important financial priority because the odds of becoming disabled before retirement can exceed the odds of dying, and the policy replaces part of income if illness or injury stops work."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"do i need disability insurance\" \"unable to work\" income)","reason":"Search for dedicated 'do I need disability insurance' pages that directly answer the need for coverage using income replacement when someone is unable to work."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"do i need disability insurance\" \"unable to work\" income)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_1034570332#0_1749595188","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1188","rank":1,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_1034570332#0_1749595188\" , \"end_char\": 675.000000 , \"headings\": \"Do I Need Disability Insurance? Do I Need Disability Insurance?\" , \"segment\": \"Do I Need Disability Insurance? | Insurance | Spending & Saving | Topics | 360 Degrees of Financial Literacy<cover>Do I Need Disability Insurance? The decision to buy disability insurance depends on your financial situation. If you are unable to work and don’t have enough savings or other income </cover>to cover your expenses, disability insurance can be a lifesaver. Types of disability insurance include: Social Security Disability Insurance. To qualify, you must have: Been employed in a job in which you paid into Social Security. A medical condition that meets the Social Security definition of total disability. Those who are only partially or temporarily disabled aren’t eligible.\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"Do I Need Disability Insurance? | Insurance | Spending & Saving | Topics | 360 Degrees of Financial Literacy\" , \"url\": \"http://www.360financialliteracy.org/Topics/Insurance/Disability-Insurance/Disability-Income-"}}
{"request":{"judgments":"40/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_1034570332#0_1749595188","relevance":3,"reason":"The document is explicitly titled 'Do I Need Disability Insurance?' and directly answers that if someone is unable to work and lacks enough savings or other income to cover expenses, disability insurance can be a lifesaver.","learned":"Disability insurance is a smart investment for people without sufficient savings or alternate income because it can cover expenses when they are unable to work."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1188","reason":"Continue this dedicated 'Do I Need Disability Insurance?' query because it is likely to retrieve more direct evidence explaining why coverage is valuable when income stops."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1188"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_02_400690911#2_698702889","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1188","rank":2,"snippet":"they be able to pay their mortgage? Would their kids still have a college savings account? Would they be able to retire? \"Your ability to earn an <cover>income is your greatest asset, and if you don't cover that, all of those other plans are at risk,\" says Kamilah Williams-Kemp, vice president for new business at Northwestern Mutual. [ Read: Alternatives to Long-Term Care Insurance. ] Many people don't like to envision a life in which they become disabled and are unable to work, but there's evidence that they should consider their options. More than 1 in 4 of today's 20-year-olds will become disabled before reaching age 67, according to a fact sheet from the Social Security Administration. For many of those workers, the presence of a solid disability plan could spell the difference between maintaining their standard of living or diving into financial insecurity.\" , \"start_char\": 935.000000 , \"title\": \"Do I Need Disability Insurance? | </cover>Family Finance | US News\" , \"url\": \"http://money.usnews.com/money/personal-finance/articles/2013/10/09/why-you-probably-need-more-disability-"}}
{"request":{"judgments":"41/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_02_400690911#2_698702889","relevance":3,"reason":"The US News document is titled 'Do I Need Disability Insurance?' and directly explains why it is valuable: earning income is a person's greatest asset, other financial plans are at risk without coverage, more than 1 in 4 young workers may become disabled before retirement, and disability insurance can help maintain standard of living rather than falling into financial insecurity.","learned":"Disability insurance is a smart investment because it protects earning ability—the asset that supports mortgages, college savings, retirement, and standard of living—against a substantial risk of disability before retirement."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1188","reason":"Continue the dedicated 'Do I Need Disability Insurance?' result list because it is producing high-quality, direct evidence explaining why coverage is financially valuable."}}
