{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_2062771509#7_3383750369","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment from a dedicated Guardian article comparing short-term and long-term disability insurance. It directly states that short-term disability is essential financial protection when savings are insufficient and that long-term disability protects financial wellbeing and retirement plans if a permanent disability prevents work.","learned":"Repeated Guardian evidence: disability insurance is smart because it protects both near-term expenses and long-term financial wellbeing/retirement plans when disability interrupts work."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"disability insurance\" \"standard of living\" \"financial insecurity\")","reason":"Search for more dedicated disability insurance evidence explaining that coverage helps maintain standard of living and avoid financial insecurity if disability prevents work."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"disability insurance\" \"standard of living\" \"financial insecurity\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_02_400690911#3_698704674","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1194","rank":1,"snippet":"Reduce Your Insurance Costs \" , \"segment\": \"[ Read: Alternatives to Long-Term Care Insurance. ] Many people don't like to envision a life in which they become disabled and are unable to work, but there's evidence that they should consider their options. More than 1 in 4 of today's 20-year-olds will become disabled before reaching age 67, according to a fact sheet from the Social Security Administration. For many of those workers, the presence of a solid disability plan could spell the difference between maintaining their <cover>standard of living or diving into financial insecurity. But purchasing disability insurance </cover>isn't always baked into our consumer habits, like buying auto insurance, life insurance or homeowners insurance, and some workers might assume that their workplace insurance or Social Security disability insurance will protect them if things get bad enough. Unfortunately, it's not that simple. Here's what to know about disability insurance. What Is Disability Insurance? In exchange for regular premium payments, disability insurance commits to paying out a portion of your salary in the event of a disabling condition. \"\" , \"start_char\": 1336.000000 , \""}}
